<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Kuku.jpg" alt="Kuku is the Swahili word for chicken" width="450" height="437" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Kuku. 12x12, oil on linen panel. 2015</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This is one of those paintings that was stuck in my head and had to get out. &nbsp;The main idea behind the orange background was to do a painting that would complement the blue green in Portrait of 817. &nbsp;Although I didn't set out to have the orange so dominant, when I left parts of the background unpainted those areas competed with the bird for attention.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">More time was spent on edges than anything else. Breaking with realism and abstracting the edges in a few places helped make the portrait more interesting.</span></p>